# Privacy Policy - PurrPair

**Last Updated:** September 20, 2026

## Summary

PurrPair has no accounts and never asks for your name, e-mail or phone number. We collect anonymous usage statistics to improve the game, purchases are handled by Apple and Google, and leaderboards are optional. There are no ads and no advertising SDKs, and we never track you across other apps or websites.

## What we collect

To understand how the game is played we use **Google Analytics for Firebase**. It records:

- Gameplay events: rounds started and ended, score, duration, difficulty, level
- Economy events: coins earned and spent, garden decorations placed, areas unlocked, daily gifts claimed, shop screens opened, completed purchases
- Technical context: app version, device model, operating system, language, country and city derived from your IP address

These records are tied to a randomly generated installation identifier, not to you. We do not collect your name, e-mail, address, contacts, photos or precise location, and we do not use an advertising identifier (IDFA / GAID). Deleting the app invalidates the identifier; reinstalling creates a new one.

## What stays on your device

Your settings, high scores, level and XP, coin balance, garden layout, collected cats and purchase entitlements are stored locally through your device's own storage. This save data is not uploaded to us.

## Purchases

In-app purchases are processed entirely by the App Store or Google Play. We never see your card details or billing address. The store tells the app which product was bought so the content can be delivered; the completed purchase is also counted in the anonymous statistics above.

## Leaderboards (optional)

If you open the leaderboard, the game uses Game Center (iOS) or Google Play Games (Android). Signing in is your choice; if you do, your score and level are submitted to that service under Apple's or Google's own privacy policies. Declining costs you nothing else in the game.

## Links and sharing

Rating the game or sharing a score opens your store page or your device's own share sheet. What you do there is handled by that app or service, not by us.

## Who processes the data

Google processes the analytics data on our behalf ([Google Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy)). Apple and Google process purchases and leaderboards as the providers of those platforms. We do not sell data, we do not share it with advertisers, and no data broker receives it.

## Legal basis and retention

Where the GDPR applies, our legal basis is legitimate interest in improving the game. Analytics records are kept for the retention period configured in Firebase (up to 14 months) and are then deleted automatically.

## Children's privacy

The game is suitable for all ages. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and the statistics we collect are not linked to an identity.

## Your choices

You can stop all analytics collection by deleting the app. For questions, corrections or a deletion request, write to the address below and state the approximate date and device you played on so we can locate the anonymous records.

## Changes to this policy

If the game changes what it collects, this document and its date will be updated before the new version is released.

